    "conclusion": "The left upper rear bearing-wrench reference remains above one and changes by about 0.0205 percent in this case; contact redistribution does not remove this reference exceedance.",
    "contact": "fixed material-point direct face-contact kinematics with small-strain internal operators and unchanged material pairs; not a closest-point contact model or a full finite-frame reassembly",
    "material_reference": {
      "Fe90_diameter_basis": "Nominal fastener diameter for each axis: 12.7 mm for the lumber-leg axes and 9.525 mm for the rail-rear axes. The smaller local root diameter does not increase Fe90 absent a source rule supporting that favorable change. Frozen V1 used local-D Fe90 and remains separately bound; V2 recomputes all 24 states on the nominal-D basis.",
      "bearing": "Local projected width D(s) times NDS Fe_parallel/Fe90 per receiver cell, divided by 5, in the source-rotated conservative ellipse. Fe_parallel and Fe90 use each axis's source-bound nominal diameter; force and first moment stay aggregate over the physical receiver.",
      "ellipse_relation": "The reciprocal-strength weighted RMS is no smaller than the Hankinson weighted mean, so the ellipse is no stronger than Hankinson at any load direction.",
      "finite_grid": "A finite-grid witness index above one is not a lower bound over all continuous fields and does not prove physical failure.",
      "matched_mode_basis": "For D>=1/4 in and theta<=90 degrees, the pinned NDS Table 12.3.1B reductions are at most 5 (Im/Is), 4.5 (II), and 4 (IIIm/IIIs/IV). Thus Fe/5 is no greater than the bearing term in each applicable matched mode, while Mp/4 is no greater than the hinge term in hinge modes; bearing-only modes have no Mp term. The separately pinned 18-control replay, including 12 hinge-governed controls, has maximum ratio 1.0. This is a conditional matched-mode material reference, not an NDS generalized wrench/group capacity formula.",
      "plastic_hinge": "Piecewise Fyb*D(s)^3/6/4; matched-mode support is bound to the prior 18-row calibration (12 hinge-governed controls).",
      "separate_metal": "Independent Fy/2 sufficient envelope is recomputed on each selected witness with actual point-action N/T and continuous lateral V/M extrema; Fy and Fyb remain separate inputs.",
